<!--
    RE-friction round 2, need `void-callee-spurious-arg`, challenge
    68149b8a8f555589f353117c (Mach-O arm64 `practice_2_rengr`): one kuna output
    contradicted itself.  The header declared `int _secret_function(void);` and
    the body of `_main` called `_secret_function(v3);`, where `v3` was the
    return value of the preceding `scanf`.  The export does not recompile, and
    an agent reading it cannot tell whether the callee consumes the value.

    Root cause (P4, active-input trial scoring).  `ActionActiveParam` recovers
    an unlocked callee's argument list from the CALLER's data flow alone
    (`FuncCallSpecs::checkInputTrialUse`, fspec.cc:5592): the ABI's first
    argument register holds a value the caller wrote and does not otherwise
    use, and `AncestorRealistic::enterNode` answers pop_solid for a Varnode
    defined by a CALL.  On AArch64 the return register and the first argument
    register are the same `x0`, so the previous call's result IS the next
    call's argument as far as the caller can see.  `calleearity` /
    `calleearityfwd` cannot help: they reconcile against a SIBLING call to the
    same callee, they are only ever additive, and here there is one call site.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 "active-input-trial-scoring".  The P0 assertion
    `option calleedeadarg on|off` decides whether a bounded decode of the
    CALLEE's own body may veto the trial: a register the callee provably
    overwrites, on every path from its entry and before ever reading it, is
    dead there and cannot be carrying an argument.

    The fixture is the same construct, hand assembled: `caller` calls
    `producer` (which returns 7 in w0) and then `target`, which overwrites x0
    with 1 before returning and so never reads it.

    Pass 1 (`option calleedeadarg off`) reproduces the BUG: `target` is called
    with the producer's return value.
    Pass 2 (`option calleedeadarg on`, the shipped default) is the FIX: the
    argument is gone and the producer's return value has no consumer.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000">
fd7bbfa9fd0300910600009407000094
00008052fd7bc1a8c0035fd61f2003d5
e0008052c0035fd6200080d2c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="caller"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100020" name="producer"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100028" name="target"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>parse line extern int4 producer(void);</com>
  <com>option calleedeadarg off</com>
  <com>lo fu caller</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option calleedeadarg on</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="calleedeadarg #1: option off passes the previous call's return value to a callee that never reads it (bug reproduced)" min="1" max="1">target\(producer\(\)\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleedeadarg #2: option on drops the argument the callee's own body proves it never reads" min="1" max="1">target\(\);</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="calleedeadarg #3: with the argument gone the producer call stands on its own (only the fixed pass)" min="1" max="1">producer\(\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
